## Stream-rule patterns (embedded `stream_rules.toml`)

- **Location:** `crates/jinn-preferences-config/src/stream_rules.toml` (one
  file; every entry carries its own `# source:` / `# license:` comment pair)
- **Licenses:** see the per-entry comments — MIT (SWE-agent), Apache-2.0
  (openai/codex), AGPL-3.0 (jinn's own shipped defaults), and unlicensed
  patterns shipped with per-entry credit by decision

Command-guard patterns adapted from:

- **dylancaponi/claude-code-permissions** — most of the shipped entries.
  No license file exists upstream; the patterns are short, ordinary regexes
  that would be re-derived to the same form, and each entry credits the
  source it came from.
- **openai/codex** (`codex-rs` command-safety checks) — Apache-2.0.
- **SWE-agent/SWE-agent** (`sweagent/tools/tools.py` blocklist) — MIT.
- **jinn's original five** (`default_jinn.toml`, this project, AGPL-3.0).
- The remainder are unattributable command-line folklore (the `curl | sh`
  class and the Steam `rm -rf "$STEAMROOT/"*` incident).
